IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`
IMPORT `cb5-schedule-offences`

-- TESTS of cb5-schedule-offences.l4 (the Schedule). Every expected value is written from the text of the
-- Schedule (src:3380-3541) before the run; none is copied from the module's output. The counts were made a
-- second way from the text: item 1 has 128 lines worth 149 provisions; items 2 to 8 have 1, 8, 5, 3, 11, 4
-- and 13.

§ `Tests of the Schedule`

§§ `How many provisions each item lists`

#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in item 1 of the Schedule` EQUALS 149
#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in item 2 of the Schedule` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in item 3 of the Schedule` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in item 4 of the Schedule` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in item 5 of the Schedule` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in item 6 of the Schedule` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in item 7 of the Schedule` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in item 8 of the Schedule` EQUALS 13
#ASSERT count `the offence provisions listed in items 1 to 8 of the Schedule` EQUALS 194

